<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 2.6 pct in November - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 2.6 pct in November - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   NOV 96     OCT 96   (NOV 95)</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.3	  0.1	(0.6)</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     2.6	  3.0	(6.0)</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    104.8	104.5    (116.5)</p>
<p>Note: The 1996 data is based on a new basket of goods. The 1995 data was collated under an old basket.</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 2.7 percent for November.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.6	   -0.1	   +3.0</p>
<p> Clothing			 105.7	   +0.3	   +3.5</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   106.9	   +0.9	   +4.9</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 104.8	   +0.6	   +2.4</p>
<p> Health spending		102.7	   +0.1	   +2.0</p>
<p> Transport			105.7	   +0.7	   +2.0</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.6	   +0.1	   +1.9</p>
<p> Education			107.0	   +1.6	   +2.6</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  104.9	   +0.2	   +3.4</p>
<p> Other goods,service	  103.0	    0.0	   +1.1</p>
<p>(including communications)</p>
</text>
